=== PART A: where does Phi itself enter the static action? (sympy) ===
  (a) Y(psi+C)-Y(psi) = 0;  clock P.grad ln N shift residual = 0
  (b) L_J(psi+C) - e^(C/c^2) L_J(psi) = 0   (J sector: Phi enters only through sqrt(-g)=N, a 1+O(Phi/c^2) factor)
  (c) d2/dC2 L_K at C=0 = 4*mu**2*cosh(psi(x, y, z)/c**2)/c**4 (nonzero: K(Q) is the only non-shift-covariant term)
      weak-field dL_K/dphi = 4*mu**2*phi/c**4  -> field-equation term linear in phi with coefficient ~ mu^2 (H2's dust, free zero point)
